Step 9: Understanding Availability Sets

The module explained Availability Sets in detail.

Fault Domains

Protect against hardware failures.

Example:

Rack Failure

Only one VM is affected.

Update Domains

Protect against planned maintenance.

Example:

Azure updates servers in stages

Not all VMs reboot simultaneously.

Benefits:
Increased availability
Reduced maintenance impact
Step 10: Understanding Availability Zones

A major focus of the module was Availability Zones.

Availability Zones are physically separate datacenters within a region.

Benefits:
Independent power
Independent cooling
Independent networking
Example:
East US

Zone 1
Zone 2
Zone 3

Applications remain available even if one zone fails.

Key concepts learned:
Availability Zones provide higher resiliency than Availability Sets
Zones support disaster recovery strategies
