Key Takeaway

Azure Virtual Machines provide flexible, scalable Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) computing resources for cloud workloads. By properly planning deployments, selecting appropriate VM sizes, implementing availability solutions, and configuring backup protection, Azure Administrators can build resilient, secure, and highly available environments that support both business-critical and development workloads. Understanding VM deployment, availability, and backup strategies is essential for success on the AZ-104 exam.
